14-## Quickstart: 
15-
16-**Prerequisites**: To run the quickstart demo, your server should have 1 GPU and the [docker environment](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/) installed.
17-
18-**Step 1:** Pull docker images
19-```bash
20:docker pull apostacyh/vllm:lmcache-0.1.0
21-```
22-
23:**Step 2:** Start vLLM + LMCache 
24-```bash
25-model=mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2    # Replace with your model name
26-sudo docker run --runtime nvidia --gpus '"device=0"' \
27:    -v <Huggingface cache dir on your local machine>:/root/.cache/huggingface \
28-    -p 8000:8000 \
29-    --env "HF_TOKEN=<Your huggingface access token>" \
30-    --ipc=host \
31-    --network=host \
32:    apostacyh/vllm:lmcache-0.1.0 \
33-    --model $model --gpu-memory-utilization 0.6 --port 8000 \
34:    --lmcache-config-file /lmcache/LMCache/examples/example-local.yaml
35-```
36:Please fill `Huggingface cache dir on your local machine` and `Your huggingface access token` in the above command. 
37-
38-You can also change the `model` variable to use different models.
39-
40:The vLLM engine is ready after you see the logs like this:
41-```
42-INFO:     Started server process [865615]
43-INFO:     Waiting for application startup.
44-INFO:     Application startup complete.
--
46-```
47-
48-**Step 3:** Run demo application
49-
50:You can now run the demo application in the LMCache repo. Please execute the following commands on the server
51-```bash
52:git clone https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache
53:cd LMCache/examples/
54-
55-# Install openai client library
56-pip install openai
57-
--
