SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold as stated. L0 shows TBA wins only under severe cache starvation: cap_frac=0.25 gives +0.0071 hit rate and -7,253 recomputed tokens, cap_frac=0.50 gives +0.0014 hit rate. It loses at cap_frac=1.0 and 1.5 with -0.0142 to -0.0173 hit rate and +14,507 to +17,664 recomputed tokens. Artifact is CPU-only synthetic simulation, 40 sessions x 8 turns, 3 seeds, no real vLLM/TensorRT-LLM GPU serving, scheduler behavior, batching, chunked prefill, tenant mix, or real agent traces.
RATIONALE: prompt_version=v001. A shipping system already exposes the core mechanism: TensorRT-LLM documents prioritized LRU and token-range retention policies, including assigning high priority to first prompt/system tokens and separate decode-token priority. The proposed "pin system + tool-schema, evict scratch first" is therefore expressible as existing retention-policy configuration, not a new systems design. The only potentially useful finding is the negative crossover: conversational scratch is later reused, so a two-class scratch-first policy damages locality when cache has headroom. That finding is supported only by L0 synthetic metrics above and is insufficient evidence for a systems claim without GPU validation on real traces and baselines against TensorRT-LLM retention policies plus SGLang priority eviction.
